# Verdict

The hoped-for "geometric symmetry repairs computability" phenomenon is real in discrete time.

For one finite rational reversible Markov chain:

\[
\boxed{
\text{exact halfspace crossing and hyperplane hitting are decidable in every dimension}.
}
\]

The reason is not mixing rate.

It is the elimination of complex spectral phases.

The next high-value frontier is whether this survives **switching among reversible kernels**, and why the analogous continuous-time theorem is more delicate.
